FerrionOS change to the upstream bootloader (MIT licence, kept), applied after ferrion-quiet-boot.patch, made against upstream commit f3d9261b5fc81418c259c5059f46ee7087e86ed8:
- verified boot on UEFI: the binary carries an empty 32-byte Ed25519 key slot after the marker FerrionBootKey/1, which scripts/verified-boot-sign.sh fills at image build time (VERIFIED_BOOT=1). With a key the bootloader loads usr/lib/boot/manifest and manifest.sig, checks the signature before reading the manifest, and refuses to start a kernel or initfs whose SHA-512 differs from it, with a message a quiet boot shows too; the boot environment editor (e) is not offered. With the slot empty it boots as before. The BIOS bootloader never verifies;
- uses ed25519-compact 2.6.1 (MIT) without default features, with opt_size.

